/* One key for Play and Stop (tester, 2026-11-04: "when the user hits play, the stop should glow red, so that they know
   that they can hit stop"). The shop's pattern for any play/stop pair: a key with class `ps` and two icons, `.ps-play`
   and `.ps-stop`; `.on` while playing shows the stop, glowing red, on the key's unlit face (a lit key would read as
   "playing", not "press to stop"). psKey() in main.ts keeps its name and tooltip in step. Each look's header key: the
   t-play rules in this file, skin-lcd.css and skin-luna.css. */
.ps .ps-stop, .ps.on .ps-play { display: none; }
.ps.on .ps-stop { display: block; }
