.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor .pvl > .pvl-l > .pvl-ic, .skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor .pvl-vox .vox-head { display: none !important; }
/* ---- Presets in a well, on the left, side by side (tester, 2026-11-03: the EQ's were right-aligned with big gaps;
   "they shouldn't have this like large gap … left justified, kind of in these wells"). And the photo keys in a well
   trimmed to their face: the photo's socket ring is lighter than the well and showed as a grey square round each key
   ("even in the wells … those buttons have gray backgrounds"). ---- */
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #eqwin header .os { order: -1; margin: 0 auto 0 0 !important; flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 4px !important; padding: 6px 8px;
  border-radius: 10px; background: #161514; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #242321; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon) #dock :is(.pv-editor, .bld) :is(.mgrp .capbtn, .os button) { clip-path: inset(1.5px round 5px) !important; }
/* Modulation's wells like the EQ's (tester, 2026-11-03: "we'll kind of fix them all the same"), its presets first. */
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #modwin .mgrp:not(.mend) { background: #161514 !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #242321 !important; border-radius: 10px !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #modwin .mpre { gap: 4px !important; }
/* ---- The screen as a piece of glass (tester, 2026-11-03: "that same very subtle bevel … like a piece of glass display
   … outset is better … illuminated from behind"): one layer over the whole right side (the takes bar, the waveform,
   the lanes, an open editor). ::before: a raised bevel (the top and left edges catch the light, the bottom and right
   fall away, a black rim) and a faint sheen from the top left. ::after: the backlight, a soft cool glow in the middle
   that falls off to darker corners. Plain alpha, no blend modes: it sits over animated canvases. ---- */
body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) .pv.ttrack::before, body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) .pv.ttrack::after {
  content: ''; position: absolute; pointer-events: none; left: calc(2px + var(--lc) + var(--gap-lcd)); top: 2px; right: 2px; bottom: 2px; border-radius: 3px; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) .pv.ttrack::after { z-index: 34;
  background: radial-gradient(70% 80% at 50% 42%, rgba(150, 190, 210, .055), rgba(150, 190, 210, .02) 55%, rgba(150, 190, 210, 0) 75%),
    radial-gradient(130% 130% at 50% 45%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 58%, rgba(0, 0, 0, .28) 100%); }
body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) .pv.ttrack::before { z-index: 35;
  background: linear-gradient(162deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, .045), rgba(255, 255, 255, .012) 22%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 40%);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, .13), inset 1px 0 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, .06), inset -1px 0 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, .45), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, .6),
    inset 0 2px 1px -1px rgba(255, 255, 255, .05), 0 0 0 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, .9), 0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, .6); }
/* The neon look draws Build's tracks as outlines, not solid (tester, 2026-11-03: "if you go neon, the track should be
   outlined instead of solid"): each hit's wave and block a 1 px line in the track's colour over a faint fill. */
body.keys-neon #dock .bld svg .bl-b { fill-opacity: .07; stroke-width: 1; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; }
body.keys-neon #dock .bld svg .bl-w .bl-wc { opacity: .18; }
body.keys-neon #dock .bld svg .bl-wb { opacity: .05; }
/* ---- Inside the screen, controls are digital, not physical (tester, 2026-11-03: "all of the different things inside
   of it are digital. They're not physical … they should have sort of a digital presence"). In the photo-key looks too,
   an editor's keys (tabs, shapes, presets, bands) are drawn on the glass: a faint fill and a thin outline, and when on,
   the track's colour with a soft glow. The flat and neon looks already draw them so. The lane arrows lose their ring
   ("people know to click on those things"). ---- */
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) #dock .pv-editor :is(.mgrp .capbtn, .capbtn, .os button) {
  border-image: none !important; clip-path: none !important; filter: none !important; transform: none !important; border-radius: 6px !important;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .025) !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, .13) !important; color: #b9bdc3 !important; text-shadow: none !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) #dock .pv-editor :is(.mgrp .capbtn, .capbtn, .os button)::after { display: none !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) #dock .pv-editor :is(.mgrp .capbtn, .capbtn, .os button):hover:not(.on) {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .05) !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, .26) !important; color: #e8eaed !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) #dock .pv-editor :is(.mgrp .capbtn, .capbtn, .os button):is(.on, :active) {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 14%, transparent) !important; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 72%, #fff) !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--tc, #22e6ff) !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) #dock .pv-editor :is(.mgrp .capbtn, .capbtn, .os button) :is(svg, span) { color: inherit !important; filter: none !important; }
.skin-lcd .pv .sec-chev { box-shadow: none !important; }
/* The Duck to keys keep their track's colour (--dc), lit in it too. */
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) #dock .pv-editor .mgrp .capbtn.duckb { color: var(--dc) !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) #dock .pv-editor .mgrp .capbtn.duckb:is(.on, :active) { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--dc) 16%, transparent) !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--dc) !important; }
/* Presets in the editor's header (tester, 2026-11-03: "presets just live in that banner at the top"): a row of small
   keys after the name, no well. The name says which is picked ("EQ: Warm"). */
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor > .ed-h .ed-pre { display: flex; align-items: center; min-width: 0; margin-left: 14px; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor > .ed-h .ed-pre :is(.os, .mpre) { display: flex !important; flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 4px !important; margin: 0 !important; padding: 0 !important; min-height: 0 !important;
  background: none !important; box-shadow: none !important; border-radius: 0 !important; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor > .ed-h .ed-pre .mpre > em { display: none !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor > .ed-h .ed-pre :is(.os button, .capbtn) { height: 22px !important; padding: 0 9px !important; font-size: 10.5px !important; }
/* The picked preset in the flat and neon looks: lit like their other keys (the photo key's dark text made it blank). */
:is(body.keys-flat, body.keys-neon).skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor .os button.on { border-image: none !important; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 14%, #121110) !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--tc, #22e6ff), 0 0 8px color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 35%, transparent) !important; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 72%, #fff) !important; text-shadow: none !important; }
/* ---- The header as the panel below it (tester, 2026-11-03: "the left side has the same … sampler look, so it looks
   continuous … the black area is like an inset display, so same as the bottom … the chop pads can be a digital
   button"): its left box on the panel material, its display the screen's colour and backlight under the same glass
   (raised bevel, sheen), the Chop Pads key drawn on the glass. The "…" stays as it is. Not in the LUNA look. ---- */
body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) > header .hd-left { background: var(--plate) !important; box-shadow: var(--plate-edge) !important; border-radius: var(--plate-r) !important; border-image: none !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) > header::before { border-radius: 3px !important;
  background: radial-gradient(70% 160% at 50% 45%, rgba(150, 190, 210, .05), rgba(150, 190, 210, .018) 55%, rgba(150, 190, 210, 0) 78%),
    radial-gradient(130% 260% at 50% 45%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 58%, rgba(0, 0, 0, .3) 100%), var(--screen, #131211) !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) > header::after { content: ''; position: absolute; z-index: 5; pointer-events: none; left: calc(2px + var(--lc) + var(--gap-lcd)); top: 2px; right: 2px; bottom: 2px; border-radius: 3px;
  background: linear-gradient(170deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, .045), rgba(255, 255, 255, .012) 35%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 60%);
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, .13), inset 1px 0 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, .06), inset -1px 0 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, .45), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, .6),
    0 0 0 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, .9), 0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, .6); }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) > header .hd-right #padsbtn { width: 34px !important; height: 34px !important; border-image: none !important; clip-path: none !important; filter: none !important;
  border-radius: 6px !important; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .025) !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, .13) !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) > header .hd-right #padsbtn svg { color: #b9bdc3 !important; filter: none !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) > header .hd-right #padsbtn:hover:not(.on) { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .05) !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, .26) !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) > header .hd-right #padsbtn:is(.on, :active) { background: color-mix(in srgb, #22e6ff 14%, transparent) !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #22e6ff !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) > header .hd-right #padsbtn:is(.on, :active) svg { color: color-mix(in srgb, #22e6ff 72%, #fff) !important; }

/* ==== The BPM and the loop keys a size up, in one tidy column (tester, 2026-11-03: "the bar and track cut off a little
   bit. They're a little bit too small … tighten up that area"): BPM at the top of the display, track and bar at its
   foot, clear of the glass edge; their left edges line up (the B of BPM over the loop icons). Drag the BPM up or down
   to change the tempo (main.ts), so it shows a vertical-resize cursor. ==== */
.skin-lcd > header .bpmwrap { margin: 0 0 0 14px !important; }
.skin-lcd > header .bpmtext { font: 500 10.5px/13px -apple-system, sans-serif !important; padding: 1px 6px !important; cursor: ns-resize !important; touch-action: none; user-select: none; -webkit-user-select: none; }
.skin-lcd > header .bpmtext.drag { color: #24edff !important; background: #000 !important; }
.skin-lcd > header .looppair { margin: 0 0 6px 14px !important; gap: 2px !important; }
.skin-lcd > header .lpbtn { height: 17px !important; min-width: 58px; font: 500 10px -apple-system, sans-serif !important; padding: 0 6px !important; gap: 5px !important; border-radius: 3px; }
.skin-lcd > header .lpbtn svg { width: 11px !important; height: 11px !important; }

/* ==== The Modulation window's controls in one row (tester, 2026-11-03, "volume gets cut off here": on the Level tab the
   Duck to keys and their Release wrapped to a second row, under the window's edge). The groups and dials a little
   tighter, and the bin goes up to the right end of the tabs' row, so Amount · shape · draw · Duck to fit across. ==== */
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor #modwin { position: relative !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #modwin .mctl { flex-wrap: nowrap !important; gap: 6px !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #modwin .mctl > .mgrp { gap: 4px !important; padding: 6px !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #modwin .mctl > .mgrp .kn2 { --kw: 42px; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #modwin .mctl > .mgrp.mend { position: absolute; right: 14px; top: 8px; padding: 0 !important; min-height: 0 !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #modwin .mctl > .mgrp.mend .capbtn { width: 24px !important; height: 24px !important; }

/* ==== Stutter's editor, inline in the screen like Modulation's (tester, 2026-11-03): its hits on a beat grid filling the
   space, the dials in one row of wells under it, the bin up at the right end of the header row's line. ==== */
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor #stutwin { position: relative !important; inset: auto !important; display: flex !important; flex-direction: column; flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 0; background: none !important; z-index: auto; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor #stutwin .stw { width: auto !important; flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 0; gap: 8px; padding: 8px 14px !important; border-radius: 0 !important; background: transparent !important; box-shadow: none !important; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor #stutwin .stw > header { display: none !important; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor #stutwin .sthost { flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 90px; height: auto; background: var(--t-data, #141312) !important; border-radius: 6px; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #stutwin .mctl { flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 6px; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #stutwin .mctl > .mgrp:not(.mend) { gap: 4px; padding: 6px 8px; min-height: 64px; box-sizing: border-box; background: #161514 !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #242321 !important; border-radius: 10px !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #stutwin .mctl > .mgrp > em { display: none; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #stutwin .mctl > .mgrp .kn2 { --kw: 48px; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #stutwin .mctl > .mgrp.mend { align-self: flex-end; padding: 0 !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor #stutwin .mctl > .mgrp.mend .capbtn { width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor #stutwin .note { display: block !important; margin: 0; font: 400 10.5px/1.35 -apple-system, sans-serif; color: #716e6a; }

/* ==== Dials the size of the keys beside them (tester, 2026-11-03: "these dials should be the same size as the squares …
   kind of like symbolical"), their names in full ("Amou…", "Spee…", "Relea…" were cut). ==== */
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor :is(#modwin, #stutwin) .mgrp .kn2 { --ks: 28px; --kw: 28px; flex: none; width: auto !important; min-width: 28px; padding: 0 1px; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor :is(#modwin, #stutwin) .mgrp .kn2 .kdial { width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv-editor :is(#modwin, #stutwin) .mgrp .kn2 .kl { max-width: none !important; overflow: visible !important; text-overflow: clip !important; white-space: nowrap; }
/* A curve across bars (tester, 2026-11-03): which bar of it is on screen, over the curve's corner. */
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor #modwin .mcurve { position: relative; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-editor #modwin .mspanl { position: absolute; right: 10px; top: 6px; z-index: 2; pointer-events: none; font: 500 10px -apple-system, sans-serif; color: #8a9097; }
/* The … menu over the header's glass (tester, 2026-11-03, "this is broken the menu": its top row went under the glass,
   which sits at z 5 over the display; the menu's corner was at z 1). */
.skin-lcd > header .hd-right { z-index: 6 !important; }

/* ==== The step's switches (Direction, Retrig, Play, Stutter) are digital buttons (tester, 2026-11-03: "should all be
   digital buttons, because that's the commitment we made … everything that's analog was on the left"): the chop's row
   sits in the screen, so its keys are drawn like the editors', outlined on the glass, lit in the track's colour. ==== */
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) .pv .tstep .dirkeys.swk button {
  border-image: none !important; border-image-source: none !important; filter: none !important; transform: none !important; border-radius: 6px !important;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .025) !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, .13) !important; color: #b9bdc3 !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) .pv .tstep .dirkeys.swk button::after { display: none !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) .pv .tstep .dirkeys.swk button:hover:not(.on) {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .05) !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, .26) !important; color: #e8eaed !important; }
body.skin-lcd:not(.keys-flat, .keys-neon, .theme-luna) .pv .tstep .dirkeys.swk button:is(.on, :active) {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 14%, transparent) !important; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 72%, #fff) !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--tc, #22e6ff) !important; }

/* ---- One device (tester, 2026-11-04: "that grayish border … the thing that attaches everything … the gaps … super tight,
   like all the gaps should look like" the 2 px seam between the panel's own cells). The grey plate (the panel's old
   bezel) runs round the whole window, 5 px; on it the header, the panel and the tracks are one black chassis: 2 px seams
   between them (each overlaps the one above by its own 2 px rim, so the seam is single), every module with its black
   rim. The resize handle is the seam itself (its grab area a little taller than it looks). ---- */
body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) { background: radial-gradient(130% 120% at 50% 4%, #2b2a28 0%, #2f2e2b 45%, #353331 100%) fixed !important; }
/* Touching modules share one seam (tester, 2026-11-04: "when you have multiple borders matching each other, you should reduce
   them by 50%"): the header reaches 2 px over the panel (the panel is pinned to its area's top, so it can't move up). */
.skin-lcd > header { margin: 5px 5px -2px !important; }
.skin-lcd main > .dockhold { margin: 0 5px !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock { padding: 0 !important; background: none !important; box-shadow: none !important; border-radius: 4px !important; }
.skin-lcd #dock .pv { border-radius: 4px !important; }
.skin-lcd #split { height: 0 !important; margin: 0 5px !important; z-index: 7 !important; }
.skin-lcd #split::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: -5px; bottom: -5px; }
.skin-lcd #lower { margin: -2px 5px 5px !important; padding: 8px 16px 14px !important; border-radius: 4px;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px #020202, inset 0 0 0 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, .55) !important; }
.skin-lcd #grid { padding-top: 4px !important; }

/* ---- The track's keys, round 4 (tester, 2026-11-04: "solo, just make it an S … one more that's mute, an M … preview is
   just play, like the same play buttons at the top … loop should just look like a loop icon … sample … use that whole
   width"): four square-ish keys, S · M · ▶/■ · Loop, then Sample with the sample's name across all four. S lights green
   (it's the one to notice), M amber; ▶ is green, and while LUNA plays the key shows the red ■ unlit, like the header's. ---- */
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell { display: grid !important; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)) !important; gap: 6px !important; align-content: end !important; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell :is(.pv-mini, .tbtns) { display: contents !important; }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-mini .pv-sq { width: 100% !important; height: 36px !important; aspect-ratio: auto !important; grid-column: auto !important; padding: 0 !important;
  display: flex !important; align-items: center !important; justify-content: center !important; font: 700 13px -apple-system, sans-serif !important; }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-mini .pv-sq svg { width: 15px !important; height: 15px !important; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-mini .pv-loop svg { fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.7; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-s { --tc: #34d35f; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-m { --tc: #ffb547; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-mini .ps .ps-play { fill: #2fd05a; filter: drop-shadow(0 0 3px rgba(47, 208, 90, .5)); }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-mini .tkey.ps.on { border-image-source: url(img/btn/w2-off.png?v=mwpj9o89) !important; background-color: transparent !important; box-shadow: none !important; color: #ff4a4a !important; }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-mini .tkey.ps.on::after { content: none !important; }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .tbtns .pv-sample { grid-column: 1 / -1 !important; width: 100% !important; height: 30px !important; aspect-ratio: auto !important; display: flex !important; align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: flex-start !important; gap: 5px !important; padding: 0 10px 0 11px !important; text-align: left; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-sample .pv-sk { flex: none; opacity: .6; font-weight: 500; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-sample .pv-sname { flex: 1; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; text-overflow: ellipsis; font-weight: 600; }
.skin-lcd .pv .pv-tcell .pv-sample .chev { flex: none; }

/* ---- Chop's + and takes (tester, 2026-11-04: "a little bit smaller … the plus sign … smaller … I like the plus sign
   filled in, but the take shouldn't have a background … white with the border, with maybe a 20% or 10% background"):
   26 px keys; + stays the filled one to click; a take is an outline, the one in use white on a faint tint of the
   track's colour, so it says which take you're on without competing with +. ---- */
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-takes .key.hubkey { width: 26px !important; height: 26px !important; }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-takes .key.hubkey .kl { font-size: 11px !important; text-shadow: none !important; }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-takes .ci-dice.key.hubkey .kl::before { width: 13px !important; height: 13px !important; }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-takes .key.hubkey:not(.ci-dice) { background: transparent !important; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 65%, #9aa0a8) !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 28%, transparent) !important; }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-takes .key.hubkey:not(.ci-dice).on { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 15%, transparent) !important; color: #fff !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 85%, #fff) !important; }
html body.skin-lcd .pv .pv-takes .key.hubkey:not(.ci-dice):hover:not(.on) { color: #e6e8eb !important; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--tc, #22e6ff) 55%, transparent) !important; }

/* ---- The tracks framed like the panels above (tester, 2026-11-04: "make this bottom portion framed in that same GUI
   treatment"): the panel material (--plate), inside the
   chassis' 2 px black rim (drawn outside its box, so it overlaps the panel's foot: one seam). Not in the LUNA look. ---- */
body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) { --lfade-t: rgb(43, 41, 39); --lfade-b: rgb(38, 37, 35); }
html body.skin-lcd:not(.theme-luna) #lower { margin: 0 7px 7px !important; padding: 12px 18px 14px !important; border-radius: var(--plate-r); background: var(--plate) !important;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #020202, var(--plate-in) !important; border-image: none !important; }

/* ==== The LUNA look (tester, 2026-10-30, with screenshots of LUNA's mixer, timeline and plug-in browser: "would it be
   possible to do a skin that looks like Luna? As an option in the settings menu … only a skin. I want to keep my
   existing skin"; "you can also use any of the graphics that are in Luna"; "all the colors should match"). ⋯ → LUNA
   look. A theme over the display layout with the flat keys (main.ts turns those on with it). Its colours are LUNA's:
   sampled from its own screens (the cool blue-greys of the window, panels, fields, section bars and toolbar) and from
   LUNA.app/Contents/Resources/appearance/Appearance.json (grey_text, pumpkin_spice). Its keys are LUNA's own button
   bitmap (images/buttons/btn@2x.png, its orange btn_L_on@2x.png on), its knobs LUNA's black pan knob
   (images/knobs/knob_pan_black.png, the upright frame, turned like Chop Shop's pointer), its type LUNA's Oxygen (SIL
   OFL, in addon/fonts). Lit steps are clips in the track's colour, as in its timeline. Every rule starts
   body.theme-luna: off, Chop Shop's own look is exactly as it was. ==== */
@font-face { font-family: "LUNA Oxygen"; src: url(fonts/Oxygen-Bold.otf) format("opentype"); font-weight: 700; }
@font-face { font-family: "LUNA Oxygen"; src: url(fonts/Oxygen.otf) format("opentype"); font-weight: 400; }
body.theme-luna {
  --lf: "LUNA Oxygen", "Oxygen", "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;
  /* Sampled from LUNA's own screens. */
  --l-bg: #252829;       /* the window, the timeline */
  --l-panel: #2d3236;    /* panels, the search field */
  --l-field: #2f363d;    /* a track header's fields */
  --l-header: #30383e;   /* a track header */
  --l-header-sel: #3a4a52;
  --l-list-hdr: #3e4346; /* the TRACKS / GROUPS bars */
  --l-toolbar: #5d6164;  /* the top toolbar */
  --l-bar: #7d8184;      /* the mixer's section bars (INPUT, RECORD FX, UTILITY …) */
  --l-bar-hi: #898d90;
  --l-mods: #787c7f;     /* the MODIFIERS column */
  --l-ruler: #414247; --l-lane: #272a2c; --l-foot: #2f3136; --l-line: #16191a;
  --l-well: #2b2f31;     /* the transport's readout cells */
  /* From Appearance.json. */
  --l-text: #fff; --l-dim: #a1adb3; /* grey_text */ --l-orange: #ffc54a; /* pumpkin_spice */
  --l-green: #8fd14f; --l-blue: #1ea0d5; --l-red: #d0021b; --l-ink: #17191a;
  /* Its keys: the button bitmap, 9-sliced (a CSS gradient of the same face underneath while it loads). */
