   prototypes/takes-screen/bezel.py, a 9-slice: its middle is plain glass, so it stretches to the column's width), the
   pixels on the glass (main.ts paintTakeScreen, oled.ts), and Blender's reflection of a soft box over them
   (img/screen/glass.png, sheen.py, stretched: a smooth gradient). ==== */
html body.lay-acc #dock .pv .acc-takes .at-screen { grid-column: 1 / -1; position: relative; box-sizing: border-box; height: 56px; border: 7px solid transparent;
  border-image: url(img/screen/bezel.png?v=mwpj9o89) 41 fill / 7px stretch; overflow: hidden; }
html body.lay-acc #dock .pv .acc-takes .at-screen canvas { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; pointer-events: none; }
html body.lay-acc #dock .pv .acc-takes .at-screen::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: var(--glass-in); border-radius: 3px; pointer-events: none;
  background: url(img/screen/glass.png?v=mwpj9o89) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat; }
/* The track's title row goes while the Takes screen shows it (tester, 2026-11-12: "remove the top title row when this is
   open"): the screen already says the track's name, so the Takes box moves up to the top of the column. */
html body.lay-acc #dock .pv .pv-head:has(.acc-takes .at-screen) .ftitle { display: none !important; }
/* …and its row goes with it, so the Takes box sits at the top (tester, 2026-11-13: "should be aligned to the top"). */
/* (tester, 2026-11-17: "all we need room for is the current track and step information, and then 2 rows of dials and
   buttons, plus 2 rows of the chop takes … we can reclaim like maybe 80 pixels"): the last row (the tools cell, hidden
   here) is 0, not auto: as auto it took the waveform's leftover height (~30 px under the dials). Padding trimmed too. */
html body.lay-acc #dock .pv > .pv-head:has(.acc-takes .at-screen) { grid-template-rows: 0 auto auto 0 !important; }
html body.lay-acc #dock .pv .pv-head:has(.acc-takes .at-screen) .pv-takes { padding-top: 6px !important; padding-bottom: 4px !important; }
/* The header's display as the Takes screen (tester, 2026-11-12: "do the same Blender treatment for the … header display"):
   Blender's recess and black glass (img/screen/bezel.png, a 9-slice, so it fits the strip's width) and its reflection over
   the readout (img/screen/glass.png), the readout in the OLED's colours: white values with a soft glow, dim labels, the
